The Say vs. Do Score — How It Works
This is the hero feature. Here's the exact methodology:
Step 1 — Embed all public statements using sentence-transformers
Step 2 — Create vote stance descriptions:
"Voted YES on HB2853 Teacher Pay Raise Act (education)"
"Voted NO on SB1234 Medicaid Expansion (healthcare)"
Step 3 — Send potential contradictions to AI for reasoning:
Statement: "I strongly support public education funding"
Vote: "Voted NO on teacher pay raise bill"
→ AI rates contradiction 1–5 and explains why
Step 4 — Aggregate into final score (1–100)
Higher = more aligned. Lower = more contradictions found.
Step 5 — Always show confidence level based on data volume:

Fewer than 5 votes = "insufficient data"
5–15 votes = "low confidence"
15+ votes = "moderate confidence"


